IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gas-types`

-- Gas Act 1986 (UK) — GOAL 1: CONNECTION (ss 10-11).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1986-44.txt.
-- The consumer asks: "Must the gas transporter connect my premises, or keep
-- them connected, and what can I be charged?"

§ `Goal 1 — connection`

-- s 10(1)(a)
@ref s 10(1)(a)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises fall within s 10(1)(a)` r IF
        r's `in an authorised area of the transporter`
    AND r's `within 23 metres of a relevant main`

-- s 10(1)(b). Premises that also fall within (a) are treated as (a)
-- premises, so that the transporter lays the pipe (F1).
@ref s 10(1)(b)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises fall within s 10(1)(b)` r IF
        r's `in an authorised area of the transporter`
    AND r's `connectable by my own pipe`
    AND NOT (r's `within 23 metres of a relevant main`)

-- s 10(4): "he shall serve on the gas transporter a notice specifying— (a)
-- the premises ...; and (b) the day (not being earlier than a reasonable
-- time after the service of the notice) upon which the connection is
-- required to be made."
@ref s 10(4)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid notice has been served for` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `notice served on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN
        CONSIDER r's `connection day named`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT LEAST n AND r's `the day named allows a reasonable time`

-- s 10(8): "likely to exceed 75,000 therms in any period of twelve months".
@ref s 10(8)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(8) excludes` r IF
    r's `expected therms a year` GREATER THAN 75000

-- s 10(9)(a)-(c); (c) only for premises within s 10(1)(b).
@ref s 10(9)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(9) excludes` r IF
        r's `the transporter is prevented by circumstances outside its control`
    OR  r's `danger to the public despite reasonable steps`
    OR  (`the premises fall within s 10(1)(b)` r AND r's `my pipe is not fit for the purpose`)

-- s 10(10)(b)-(d): a new or increased supply, more than 2,500 therms a year
-- expected, needing a new or enlarged main or other works; the transporter
-- may refuse "unless that person enters into a written contract".
@ref s 10(10)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transporter may insist on a written contract for` r IF
        r's `a new or increased supply needing a new or enlarged main or works`
    AND r's `expected therms a year` GREATER THAN 2500
    AND NOT (r's `written contract for the transporter's payments`)

-- s 11(1): only where the pipe falls to be laid by the transporter under
-- s 10(2)(a).
@ref s 11(1)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transporter may refuse to lay the pipe for want of security for` r IF
        `the premises fall within s 10(1)(a)` r
    AND r's `security required and not given`

@ref ss 10(2)-(4), (8)-(10), 11(1)
@export Must the gas transporter connect my premises (s 10(2)), or maintain my existing connection (s 10(3)), under the Gas Act 1986 (UK)? The premises must be within 23 metres of a relevant main, or connectable by the owner's or occupier's own pipe, in the transporter's authorised area, with a notice naming the premises and a day not earlier than a reasonable time after it (s 10(4)). The duty does not apply over 75,000 therms a year (s 10(8)) or in the circumstances of s 10(9); the transporter may refuse without a written contract under s 10(10), or refuse to lay the pipe until security is given under s 11. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`  @desc Where the premises are, whether they are connected, the notice, the expected supply, and the transporter's circumstances
GIVETH A `Connection outcome`
`must the transporter connect` r MEANS
    IF r's `already connected`
    THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `s 10(8) excludes` r                                   THEN `need not: over 75,000 therms`
            IF `s 10(9) excludes` r                                   THEN `need not: circumstances under s 10(9)`
            IF `the transporter may insist on a written contract for` r THEN `may refuse until a written contract is made`
            OTHERWISE                                                     `must maintain the connection`
    ELSE
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (`the premises fall within s 10(1)(a)` r OR `the premises fall within s 10(1)(b)` r)
                                                                      THEN `the duty does not cover my premises`
            IF NOT (`a valid notice has been served for` r)            THEN `no valid notice yet`
            IF `s 10(8) excludes` r                                   THEN `need not: over 75,000 therms`
            IF `s 10(9) excludes` r                                   THEN `need not: circumstances under s 10(9)`
            IF `the transporter may insist on a written contract for` r THEN `may refuse until a written contract is made`
            IF `the transporter may refuse to lay the pipe for want of security for` r
                                                                      THEN `may refuse to lay the pipe until security is given`
            OTHERWISE                                                     `must connect`

-- s 10(5): the cost of supplying and laying the pipe, for (2)(a) premises;
-- (5A): the cost of making the connection, for (2)(b) premises. Each only
-- "if and to the extent that the transporter so requires and the conditions
-- of his licence so allow".
@ref s 10(5), (5A)
@export What can I be charged for a new connection under s 10 of the Gas Act 1986 (UK)? For premises within 23 metres of a relevant main, the cost of supplying and laying the pipe (s 10(5)); for premises connected by my own pipe, the cost of making the connection (s 10(5A)); in each case only if the transporter requires it and its licence allows. An existing connection carries no charge under s 10. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`  @desc Where the premises are and whether they are already connected
GIVETH A `Connection charge`
`the connection charge for` r MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF r's `already connected`                    THEN `no charge under s 10`
        IF `the premises fall within s 10(1)(a)` r    THEN `the cost of supplying and laying the pipe`
        IF `the premises fall within s 10(1)(b)` r    THEN `the cost of making the connection`
        OTHERWISE                                          `no charge under s 10`

-- s 10(6): on a connection under (2)(b), my pipe, and my rights and
-- liabilities about it, vest in the transporter.
@ref s 10(6)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my pipe vests in the transporter on connection for` r IF
        NOT (r's `already connected`)
    AND `the premises fall within s 10(1)(b)` r
    AND `must the transporter connect` r EQUALS `must connect`

-- s 11(2): interest is payable on an amount deposited as security under s 11.
@ref s 11(2)
GIVEN r IS A `Connection request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `interest is payable on a security deposit for` r IF
        NOT (r's `already connected`)
    AND `the premises fall within s 10(1)(a)` r
